# MANDATORY: MCTB PAGE BUILD SPEC — 11: CONSENT

**Route:** `/mctb/setup/consent` | **Wizard:** Setup Step 3 (spec 07)  
**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPEC-11-CONSENT.md`  
**Prerequisites:** Governing MCTB docs + specs 01–10, 12

## When this rule activates

**Before implementing, restyling, or declaring complete** MCTB Consent (`/mctb/setup/consent`, wizard consent step).

## Primary job

High-consequence configuration: how MCTB **establishes or relies on** permission to text missed callers.

## Two modes (LOCKED — semantically distinct)

| UI label | Enum | Evidence |
|----------|------|----------|
| Ask callers to press 1 | `press_1` | Platform-captured — DTMF 1 after voice disclosure |
| Use permission my business already has | `existing_consent` | Business attestation / external provenance — **not** Transovo-captured |

**Never:** "Skip consent", Manual/Automatic, consent = boolean

## Press-1 (`press_1`)

Voice disclosure → caller presses 1 → consent event → system SMS → opener. Do not mark captured before DTMF succeeds.

- Centralized/versioned disclosure; locked required wording where policy requires
- Preview/Publish per runtime; failed generation keeps prior active prompt
- Evidence: method, timestamp, disclosure version, source call

## Existing Permission (`existing_consent`)

Attestation checkbox — **never prechecked**. Provenance distinct from Press-1 evidence. No fake platform consent.

## Not on this page

Sender registration, A2P/TFV, message templates, opt-out override, forwarding, full Consent Log UI, AI eligibility

## Relationships

- **Text Back** — consumes mode for message sequence (no duplicate mode store)
- **Test & Diagnostics** — Press-1 checkpoints only when `press_1`
- **Missed Call Detail** — same canonical consent state
- Link to Consent History — not main nav

## Switching modes

Future events only; history immutable; opt-out not overridden; consequential confirmation

## Prohibited

Skip consent label, prechecked attestation, A2P/TFV as recipient consent, AI decides permission, second consent engine, frontend send eligibility

## Definition of done

See full spec §83 checklist.
